# Findings the secret scan raised that are NOT secrets.
#
# One line per finding, and each line is a FINGERPRINT:
#
#     <commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>
#
# That is as narrow as this file gets. It silences that one rule, on that one
# line, of that one file, in that one commit - and nothing else. A new secret on
# the next line of the same file still fails the build. Never add a bare path or
# a rule name here: either would switch the scanner off for everything it covers.
#
# Before adding a line, read the flagged line in the source and say in the
# comment WHY it is not a secret. "gitleaks is noisy" is not a reason; somebody
# has to be able to check your answer later without re-running anything.
#
